## Lore

The True Atlanteans descend from the humans of ancient Atlantis, whose ley line magic and dimensional exploration made them the first great civilization on Earth, with alliances across the Megaverse and the Chiang-Ku dragons, who gave them tattoo magic. A dimensional experiment gone wrong opened a super rift that loosed monsters, vampire intelligences and disease on the world, drained the ley lines and, two thousand years later, took the continent itself. Of sixty million people, about a million fled to other dimensions and fewer than six thousand to other lands on Earth.

Their descendants are transdimensional nomads, scattered in small clans and wandering bands, and most carry their ancestors'' guilt as a personal debt: they hunt vampires, the Splugorth and supernatural villains wherever they go, a self-appointed police force of the Megaverse. A few thousand have come back to Rifts Earth to find Atlantis risen again under the Splugorth. Some fight openly; others quietly restore the ancient pyramids and chart the ley lines. Lately an unknown enemy has been assassinating True Atlanteans across the dimensions.

Physically they are larger, stronger and longer-lived than humans, adapted to constant contact with magic and the bizarre. They are headstrong, confident and bold, usually noble, generous and honorable, and an evil Atlantean is just as determined in his wickedness. They appear entirely human: tall (six to seven feet), handsome and dark-haired.

## Occupations

A True Atlantean can take any O.C.C., though most are magic or psionic. The book''s split among adventurers: Ley Line Walker 15%, Shifter 13%, Techno-Wizard 12%, Temporal Wizard 12%, Undead Slayer 10%, Stone Master 10%, Nomad 9%, Mind Melter 5%, Mind Bleeder 4%, Mystic 2%, other or non-magic 8%. Adventurers are about 60% male. About three percent of True Atlanteans are survivors of the original Atlantis, typically 12th level or higher and not recommended as player characters. The Stone Master and Undead Slayer vary these racial abilities slightly; see their own entries.

## GM Notes

Every century or so the clans gather to trade news. The Aerihman clan has not attended for 400 years; its young leader Aerihza is rumored to dream of a new Atlantean empire and to deal with supernatural powers, though the clan has itself lost 1300 members to the unknown assassins.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'true-atlantean');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'true-atlantean';

